-- title:
--   Pointwise lower bound for the kernel on a pair of cone-restricted unit cubes
-- statement:
--   Work in Euclidean space $\mathbb{R}^d$ with the integer lattice $\mathbb{Z}^d$. Let $\Gamma$ be a configuration, let $k : \mathbb{R}^d \times \mathbb{R}^d \to [0,\infty]$ be a kernel satisfying $\mathrm{KernelBounds}(\Gamma, \alpha, \Lambda, k)$, and let $\alpha > 0$. Let $F$ be a family of reference cones for $\Gamma$ of aperture $\theta$, with $F.\mathrm{cone}\,m$ the cone indexed by $m$ and $F.\mathrm{shrunkAt}\,m\,\rho\,x$ that cone shrunk by $\rho$ and placed at $x$. Write $A_1^{V}(u) = \{ s \in A_1(u) : V \subseteq \Gamma(s)\}$ for the cone-restricted unit cube at $u$, and $\mathbf{1}_A$ for the $[0,\infty]$-valued indicator of $A$.
--
--   Let $x, y \in \mathbb{Z}^d$ be lattice points with the separation
--   $$\sqrt{d} < \|x - y\|,$$
--   let $m, n \in \mathbb{R}^d$ be arbitrary indices, and let
--   $$s \in A_1^{F.\mathrm{cone}\,m}(x), \qquad t \in A_1^{F.\mathrm{cone}\,n}(y).$$
--   Then
--   $$\Lambda^{-1}\Big(\mathbf{1}_{F.\mathrm{shrunkAt}\,m\,\sqrt{d}\,x}(y) + \mathbf{1}_{F.\mathrm{shrunkAt}\,n\,\sqrt{d}\,y}(x)\Big)\,(2\sqrt{d})^{-d-\alpha}\,\|x-y\|^{-d-\alpha} \;\le\; k(s,t).$$
--
--   The estimate replaces the pair $(s,t)$, which ranges over a product of two cubes, by the pair of lattice centres $(x,y)$: the separation hypothesis guarantees that $\|s - t\| \le 2\sqrt{d}\,\|x-y\|$ for such $s$ and $t$, which is what the factor $(2\sqrt{d})^{-d-\alpha}$ absorbs, and the indicator sum records that at least one of the two centres is seen inside the other's shrunk reference cone, which is the hypothesis under which the lower bound of the kernel assumption applies. Integrating this pointwise bound over the two cubes is what produces the lower bound for the averaged discrete kernel.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Values are in $\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}^{\infty}$ and the real factors are injected by `ENNReal.ofReal`. The indices $m, n$ carry no membership hypothesis; when the corresponding cone-restricted cubes are empty the hypotheses on $s$ and $t$ cannot be met, so the statement is vacuous for such indices.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/dbenbenn/quadratic-forms-sobolev/blob/7a1a680db2124d46ce370c91fd450aa454edf491/QuadraticFormsSobolev/Section3Kernel.lean#L177-L241

